---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 28, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for pbasa.org - what information Palm Beach Academy of Sports and Arts collects on this website, how it is used, third-party services involved, and how to contact us about your information."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="How Palm Beach Academy of Sports and Arts handles information collected through this website."
  />

  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-narrow max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-navy-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-navy-600 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Overview</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            Palm Beach Academy of Sports and Arts ("PBASA", "we", "our") operates this website at pbasa.org to
            share information about our tuition-free K-8 public charter school with families, staff, and community
            partners. We respect the privacy of everyone who visits, and we keep the amount of information we
            collect as small as possible. This policy explains what happens with information related to this
            website. It does not describe student records held by the school, which are governed by the Family
            Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and applicable Florida law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Information we collect</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            This website does not host its own accounts, logins, or on-page forms, and it does not sell any
            information. We collect information in only two ways:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-4 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-800">Information you send us.</strong> If you email contact@pbasa.org or
              employment@pbasa.org, we receive whatever you choose to include, such as your name, email address,
              phone number, and the details of your question or application.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-navy-800">Basic technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider records standard
              server information, such as IP address, browser type, referring page, and time of request, in order
              to serve pages, protect the site from abuse, and understand aggregate traffic levels.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">How we use information</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            We use what you send us to answer your question, process an employment inquiry, follow up on a
            pre-enrollment interest, or coordinate a sponsorship. We use technical data only to operate and
            secure the website. We do not use this information for advertising, and we do not sell, rent, or
            trade it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Third-party services</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            Some features link to services operated by other organizations, and their own privacy policies apply
            once you leave this site:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-4 space-y-2">
            <li>Netlify hosts this website and processes standard server logs.</li>
            <li>Google Fonts serves the typefaces used in our design.</li>
            <li>Google Forms hosts our pre-enrollment form and receives the information you submit there.</li>
            <li>GoFundMe processes donations made through our fundraising page.</li>
            <li>Google Docs and BoardDocs host certain public documents, such as the school calendar.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Cookies and tracking</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            This website does not set advertising or analytics cookies of its own and does not track visitors
            across other sites. Embedded or linked third-party services may set their own cookies when you use
            them. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time without losing access to
            the content on this site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Children's privacy</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            This website is written for parents, guardians, prospective staff, and community members rather than
            for children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through it. Student
            information collected as part of enrollment or attendance is handled by the school under FERPA and
            Florida student-records requirements, not through this website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Retention and security</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            We keep email correspondence only as long as needed to handle your request and to meet public-records
            and recordkeeping obligations that apply to Florida charter schools. The site is served over HTTPS,
            and access to our email accounts is limited to authorized staff.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Your choices</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            You may ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it,
            subject to any legal retention requirements. Email
            <a href="mailto:contact@pbasa.org" class="text-gold-600 hover:text-gold-700">contact@pbasa.org</a>
            and we will respond as promptly as we can.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            If we change how this website handles information, we will update this page and revise the date
            above. Significant changes will also be noted on our homepage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-navy-900 mb-3">Contact</h2>
          <div class="gold-divider mb-4"></div>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:contact@pbasa.org" class="text-gold-600 hover:text-gold-700">contact@pbasa.org</a>,
            or see our <a href="/contact" class="text-gold-600 hover:text-gold-700">contact page</a> for all
            available channels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
